# Incremental version control

Maintain a proper git history **as work proceeds**, not only when the user asks at the end.

## Required cadence

- After each coherent, working change (feature slice, bugfix, refactor, or config change), create a git commit before starting the next unrelated step.
- Prefer several small commits over one large dump at the end of a session.
- Do not leave a long run of finished work uncommitted in the working tree.

## Commit quality

- Follow the repo commit protocol: status/diff/log, stage only relevant files, clear message focused on why.
- Exclude secrets, backups (`*.bak*`), runtime data, cookies, and personal CV/profile dumps.
- Never amend/push unless the user explicitly asks.
- Never update git config.

## Exception

- Skip empty commits when there is nothing to record.
- If the user says not to commit yet, wait — otherwise assume step-by-step commits are required.
